# CODEOWNERS
#
# When a pull request changes a file, GitHub asks that file's owner to review
# it. That is ALL this file does. It does not stop anyone editing anything.
#
# On this repository it has no teeth at all: branch protection is unavailable
# on the current plan, and requiring code-owner review is what would give it
# force. So read this as the map each agent reads to learn where the boundary
# is, and as the record of who owns what. The control that actually protects
# main is Hassan reading the diff before he merges.
#
# THE LAST MATCHING LINE WINS. Not the most specific one. Order matters.
# A leading / anchors at the repository root. A trailing / matches everything
# inside the directory.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default. Anything not claimed below is Hassan's.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                          @zhssnym

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Imran's ground.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the user sees. Both names on purpose: with Imran alone, every client fix
# Hassan makes would sit waiting for Imran's approval, and most recent client
# commits were Hassan's. With both names, whoever did not write it can approve
# it.
#
# Component tests live in here too, beside the components they test, and are
# owned by this line. That is why app/tests/ is not split.
/app/src/client/           @mranwafa @zhssnym

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hassan's ground.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redundant with the `*` line today. They stop being redundant the moment
# anyone adds a broader rule above them, which is the whole reason to write
# them down.
/app/src/server/           @zhssnym
/app/db/                   @zhssnym
/app/tests/                @zhssnym
/.github/                  @zhssnym
/docs/spec/                @zhssnym
/docs/rfcs/                @zhssnym
/docs/workflow/            @zhssnym
/CODEOWNERS                @zhssnym

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The contested middle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The contract between the two halves. 36 server files and 59 client files
# import from it, and a change here is a change to spec section 7 in disguise.
# Reading it is free and constant; only editing it asks for a review.
#
# One standing exception, written in docs/workflow/frontend/: a frontend pull
# request may add a new READ schema for a shape the server already sends.
# Nothing on the server imports it, and a wrong one fails loudly on one screen.
# Request schemas are different and never move alone, because an unhandled
# field is accepted and silently dropped with a 200.
/app/src/shared/           @zhssnym

# Dependencies. Imran's agent will want UI libraries. That is a bundle size,
# licence and supply chain decision, so it comes here.
/app/package.json          @zhssnym
/app/package-lock.json     @zhssnym
